%% Hybrid DNS for private endpoints - three resolution flows - Contoso profile
%% Source: codex/blueprint-azure-dns-for-private-endpoints.md (Microsoft Learn: Azure DNS Private Resolver overview; Azure Private Endpoint private DNS zone values)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Contoso file server
  participant IB as Infoblox grid
  participant PUB as Public DNS
  participant IN as Resolver inbound endpoint (hub)
  participant AZ as Azure DNS 168.63.129.16
  participant Z as privatelink.file.core.windows.net
  participant VM as Azure VM (spoke)
  participant OUT as Resolver outbound endpoint + ruleset
  Note over C,Z: Flow 1 - on-premises client resolves an Azure file share
  C->>IB: account.file.core.windows.net ?
  IB->>PUB: account.file.core.windows.net ?
  PUB-->>IB: CNAME account.privatelink.file.core.windows.net
  IB->>IN: account.privatelink.file.core.windows.net ? (conditional forwarder)
  IN->>AZ: query
  AZ->>Z: lookup A record (zone linked to hub)
  Z-->>IN: A 10.x.x.x
  IN-->>IB: A 10.x.x.x
  IB-->>C: A 10.x.x.x then SMB 445 / HTTPS 443 over ExpressRoute to the private endpoint
  Note over VM,Z: Flow 2 - Azure VM resolves the same share
  VM->>AZ: account.file.core.windows.net ?
  AZ->>Z: linked zone answers
  Z-->>VM: A 10.x.x.x
  Note over VM,IB: Flow 3 - Azure VM resolves a Contoso AD name
  VM->>AZ: dc01.contoso.local ?
  AZ->>OUT: ruleset rule contoso.local. matches
  OUT->>IB: dc01.contoso.local ? (UDP/TCP 53 over ExpressRoute)
  IB-->>OUT: A 10.1.x.x
  OUT-->>VM: A 10.1.x.x
